{
  "planVersion": 1,
  "title": "Scheduled publishing",
  "summary": "Authors give a post an optional publish date and time. Until it passes, the post exists only for its author: everyone else and guests do not see it in the list, in search, or on its page. Once it passes the post is public with no further action. A console command lists what is scheduled.",
  "locale": "en",
  "scope": {
    "goals": [
      "Set, change or clear a post's publish date from the create and edit forms",
      "Hide a scheduled post from everyone but its author in the list, in search and on its page",
      "Show authors their scheduled posts in the list with the date",
      "Let ops print the scheduled posts with bun run console posts:scheduled"
    ],
    "nonGoals": [
      "Notifying anyone when a post goes public",
      "A job or timer that flips a flag at publish time; visibility is decided when the post is read",
      "Unpublishing a post that is already public by any means other than giving it a future date"
    ]
  },
  "assumptions": [
    "posts.published_at is a nullable text column holding an ISO 8601 UTC timestamp, like created_at. Null or a time at or before now means public; a later time means scheduled.",
    "The form field is publishAt: an ISO 8601 date-time with Z or an offset, normalized to UTC (toISOString) before it is stored, so the stored strings compare in time order. Absent or null means publish now (published_at null).",
    "Updating a post with publishAt absent or null clears the schedule; the edit form always sends the field.",
    "Visibility lives on the Post model as named query scopes: published (published_at null or not after now) and scheduled (published_at after now). index, show and search all read through one helper that ANDs (published OR written by the viewer) onto their own conditions, so the rule is written once.",
    "A scheduled post's page answers 404 to everyone but its author, the same as a post that does not exist, so its existence does not leak.",
    "bun run console posts:scheduled prints one line per scheduled post, <id>\\t<title>\\t<published_at>, soonest first (ties by id), through the command's plain line output, and nothing else on stdout; with nothing scheduled it prints nothing and exits 0.",
    "An invalid publishAt fails exactly as an invalid title does: 422 with errors on publishAt, nothing saved."
  ],
